    {
      "kind": "native-adaptation",
      "reason": "2026-11-01 reviewed 2.0.84 -> 2.0.88 from SRI/SHA256-verified published archives and matching-release tests 612be2311464804d1e4897afacbf8f3fc2f6d9e3 -> 9b603d36186b75e58d5479445a96c76f6e2d2700. Ported stable prompt APIs, diagnostic cause preservation and current MRTR semantics: 10 retries, 250ms state-only pacing, original/current-round params, empty state, cancellation/close/timeout coverage and no late resend. Foundation has no global fetch receiver issue; stable native MCPStdioTransport export already covers export intent. Form-only elicitation matches upstream; no broader MCP parity claim."
    },
    {
      "kind": "native-adaptation",
      "reason": "2026-11-14: Swift retains native connection-time DNS pinning for untrusted downloads. The upstream Node/Undici removal does not weaken this native transport. Explicit custom OAuth transports carry responsibility for connect-time DNS validation; native URLSession token/registration requests outside configured trust require a protected custom transport. JS Symbols/property descriptors, Zod/TypeScript inference, browser workers and workflow serialization are not native product surfaces."
    }
